  "question": {
    "text": "In a group of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>400</mn></math> people, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>160</mn></math> are smokers and non-vegetarian; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn></math> are smokers and vegetarian and the remaining <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>140</mn></math> are non-smokers and vegetarian. Their chances of getting a particular chest disorder are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>35</mn><mo>%</mo><mo>,</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>%</mo></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>%</mo></math> respectively. A person is chosen from the group at random and is found to be suffering from the chest disorder. The probability that the selected person is a smoker and non-vegetarian is :",
    "image": null
  },
